wget: use _exit() in the vfork child when openssl cannot be executed

spawn_https_helper_openssl() vforks and, if exec of "openssl" fails, the
child calls xfunc_die() -> exit(). In a vfork child that runs the parent's
atexit handlers and stdio flush in the shared address space. With musl >=
1.2.5 it is worse: exit() takes a lock keyed on the thread id, and since the
vfork child shares the parent's thread struct, the parent's own exit() later
looks like a recursive call and musl deliberately crashes (SIGSEGV on hlt).

Symptom: static musl busybox without openssl installed, every https wget
download succeeds and then dies with "Segmentation fault" (exit 139).

--- a/networking/wget.c
+++ b/networking/wget.c
@@ -742,11 +742,14 @@
 
 		BB_EXECVP(argv[0], argv);
 		xmove_fd(3, 2);
+		/* vfork child: must not call exit(), it shares the parent's
+		 * address space (atexit handlers, stdio, musl's exit lock) */
 # if ENABLE_FEATURE_WGET_HTTPS
 		child_failed = 1;
-		xfunc_die();
+		_exit(xfunc_error_retval);
 # else
-		bb_perror_msg_and_die("can't execute '%s'", argv[0]);
+		bb_perror_msg("can't execute '%s'", argv[0]);
+		_exit(xfunc_error_retval);
 # endif
 		/* notreached */
 	}
